The bug was caused by the `DisjunctionSumScorer` class calling the `score()` method on a subscorer that had already returned `NO_MORE_DOCS`, which could lead to incorrect scoring results or exceptions. This situation arises when the logic does not properly check if there are valid documents to score before attempting to access the scoring functionality.

